cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results, data or code, please cite them as below."
title: "Agent Payments Lab: open experiments on how AI agents pay"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mikhail
    family-names: Rymanov
    alias: Mike Rymanov
repository-code: "https://github.com/rymanov/agent-payments-lab"
url: "https://agentpaymentslab.com"
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered experiments on how AI agents pay and how to keep them in check. An agent asks to pay; a
  separate mandate checker holds the key and signs only what the owner's mandate allows. Each experiment's plan
  and analysis script are timestamped before its trials, a script labels every outcome, and the trial logs are
  public. Experiment E1a planted instructions to overspend, pay an unlisted supplier or pay twice, across seven
  models; it ran on mock services with an unfunded test key.
keywords:
  - agentic payments
  - AI agents
  - prompt injection
  - payment mandates
  - x402
  - stablecoins
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: "E1a"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
